 },
 "blocks": [
  {
   "id": "t0",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "A plain guide to layer 2",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 80,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t1",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Why layer 2 exists",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 124,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t2",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Layer 2 networks exist because Ethereum mainnet can only process a limited number of transactions per second, which keeps fees high when demand rises.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 168,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t3",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "How rollups work",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 212,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t4",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "A rollup executes transactions off the main chain and posts compressed data back to Ethereum. Optimistic rollups assume transactions are valid and allow a challenge window of about seven days.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 256,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t5",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Zero-knowledge rollups",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 300,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t6",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Zero-knowledge rollups instead post a cryptographic proof that the batch was computed correctly, so withdrawals can finish much faster.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 344,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t7",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Where the fees go",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 388,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t8",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Fees on a rollup have two parts: the cost of execution on the layer 2, which is tiny, and the cost of posting data to Ethereum, which dominates.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 432,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t9",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Blobs and Dencun",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 476,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t10",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Since the Dencun upgrade in March 2024, rollups post data in blobs, which cut layer 2 fees by roughly an order of magnitude.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 520,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t11",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Bridges",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 564,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t12",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Bridges move assets between chains. A canonical bridge is run by the rollup itself; third-party bridges are faster but add trust assumptions.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 608,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t13",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Sequencers",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 652,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t14",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Sequencers order transactions on most rollups today. Most are run by a single company, which is a centralisation risk the teams plan to remove.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 696,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t15",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Forced inclusion",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 740,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t16",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "If a sequencer goes offline, users can usually force transactions through the contract on Ethereum, though it is slower and costs more.",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 784,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t17",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "Choosing one",
   "inView": true,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 828,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t18",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "Choosing a layer 2 depends on what you need: low fees, fast withdrawals, the apps you want to use, or the strength of the security model.",
   "inView": false,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 872,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t19",
   "kind": "h",
   "text": "A rule of thumb",
   "inView": false,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 916,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "t20",
   "kind": "p",
   "text": "For small payments, almost any rollup is fine. For large sums, look at how decentralised the sequencer and the upgrade keys are.",
   "inView": false,
   "rect": {
    "x": 360,
    "y": 960,
    "w": 760,
    "h": 28
   }
  }
 ],
